e miniature toys have been","options":{"A":"made by the museum","B":"bought by the museum","C":"borrowed by the museum"}},{"q":16,"text":"The biscuit factory made tins","options":{"A":"for people all over the world","B":"of different shapes","C":"for many famous people"}},{"q":17,"text":"People’s favourite biscuit used to be","options":{"A":"an unsweetened one","B":"one covered in chocolate","C":"one filled with cream"}},{"q":18,"text":"The hands-on activity allows people to","options":{"A":"make some biscuits","B":"taste some of the biscuits","C":"pack a biscuit tin"}}]},{"kind":"notes","range":"Questions 19 and 20","instruction":"Complete the sentences below.","word_limit":"Write NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS for each answer.","title":"Visitor Information","items":[["The gift shop is located beside the ",{"q":19}," on the ground floor."],["Free ",{"q":20}," are available for visitors’ belongings."]]}]},{"number":3,"label":"SECTION 3","range":"Questions 21–30","blocks":[{"kind":"mcq","range":"Questions 21–24","instruction":"Choose the correct letter, A, B or C.","title":"Pacific Tapa Cloth","questions":[{"q":21,"text":"Pacific tapa cloth is different from other types because it is","options":{"A":"the only tapa made today","B":"better quality than others","C":"put to a wider range of uses"}},{"q":22,"text":"What does Helen say about the paper mulberry tree?","options":{"A":"It is also a source of food","B":"It is not native to the Pacific","C":"It can grow in any environment"}},{"q":23,"text":"Why did the Maori people of New Zealand stop making tapa?","options":{"A":"They could not find the right trees in New Zealand","B":"They were introduced to other fabrics by the Europeans","C":"They found a better material for making fabric"}},{"q":24,"text":"Large pieces of tapa are made from smaller pieces which are","options":{"A":"stuck together","B":"woven together","C":"sewn together"}}]},{"kind":"matching","range":"Questions 25–30","title":"Tapa Cloth — Functions in Different 